Stop naming the crowd —
cap the message, not the man;
count errors out loud.

Don’t seek one master token to follow far and wide;
Let consent name each purpose, with revocation by its side.

Begin with chosen anchors where logged-in signals meet;
Keep every graph partitioned, and let uncertain matches sleep.

Test joins on volunteered truth, count false links as cost;
Cap reach only above thresholds, and abstain when truth is lost.

Let channels keep their borders; send decisions, not a name;
The gaps will still be with us—we can bound, but not end, the game.
